.PP
Defined if a memory page can only ever be RW or RX, never RWX at the
same time, as enforced by the OS.
.PP
   *   *   *   *   *
.SS W_NOT_TO_X
.IP
.EX
#define W_NOT_TO_X
.EE
.PP
Defined if a page, once writable, can NEVER become executable at all (no
W\->X transition permitted by any means, not even dual\-mapping).
.PP
Stricter than W_XOR_X; only defined where that stronger guarantee holds.
.PP
